 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? You can use language app on your phone as if you were talking to someone. Pick simple phrase before you leave the room, then come back a few minutes later to see how it sounds. You can turn down the volume and keep the screen dark so it looks like nothing is happening. Or pick a quiet room and let the neighbour know what you' doing. Another way is to choose a language course app that has short daily lessons and do a few minutes each day. They' usually start with hello and how are you, which feels like real conversation. You can turn the volume down and only do one or two phrases at first. Then you can build up over days and weeks. Pick a few simple phrases like hello how are you and thank you and practice them a few times a day. You' be surprised how quickly you start to sound confident.",
